# Issue Loop Engineering

## Autonomy

- Drive progress toward MySQL 8.0 compatibility **without asking the user whether to continue**
- Keep `main` deliverable: every merge must pass CI, update user-facing docs, and document how to test new features
- Prefer small PRs that merge quickly over long-lived branches

## Session start (in order)

1. `node scripts/check-issue-replies.mjs` — process `needs-human` replies
2. `gh issue list --repo tanbamboo/rusql --label agent-ready --json number,title,labels`
3. Pick highest `priority:P0`; if none, create the next milestone issue from the roadmap
4. Follow [docs/en/workflows/spec-to-ship.md](../../docs/en/workflows/spec-to-ship.md)

## On completion

1. Run sensors: `cargo fmt`, `clippy`, `test`, `harness-validate`
2. Update [README.md](../../README.md) and [docs/en/user-guide.md](../../docs/en/user-guide.md) (and zh-CN mirror) for user-testable changes
3. Open PR, merge when CI green
4. Update HANDOFF.md; label next issue `agent-ready`

## File Boundaries

Never modify files outside the issue spec boundaries.
